From cf9ffaaf2e76ad1af5d24ed02d4402b1c66bb317 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cruz <cruz@tbu.net>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 12:25:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 132/206] fix(app_snapshot): WrapCode records cpu stats in
 non-simulator builds

The !IsLinkingEnabled() path was recording stats as sim since 1f1e51ad16e,
which fixed the B6 crash but left CPU stats at zero in ProductARM64 builds.
This was invisible when dartaotruntime was kReadOnly (macOS allowed
executing read-only pages) but was exposed once dd_runtime_check.sh
could reach the --print_shorebird_info stats section.

Use DART_INCLUDE_SIMULATOR to distinguish: Simulator builds interpret
all code (charge sim), non-Simulator builds run natively (charge cpu).
The identity wrapper and the identity return are unchanged in both cases.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/runtime/vm/app_snapshot.cc b/runtime/vm/app_snapshot.cc
index 37a31ebee5d..dd7a69fdc10 100644
--- a/runtime/vm/app_snapshot.cc
+++ b/runtime/vm/app_snapshot.cc
@@ -10033,7 +10033,13 @@ Deserializer::EntryPoints Deserializer::WrapCode(CodePtr code,
   // ARM64 — which is PROT_READ-only and faults immediately (B6 crash).
   // Identity lets the Simulator interpret the patch bytecode directly.
   if (!IsLinkingEnabled()) {
+    // In a Simulator build the code will be interpreted, so charge sim.
+    // In a native (ProductARM64) build the code runs on CPU.
+#if defined(DART_INCLUDE_SIMULATOR)
     stats_.Record(LinkOracle::RunTarget::sim, length);
+#else
+    stats_.Record(LinkOracle::RunTarget::cpu, length);
+#endif
     return EntryPoints(payload_start, identity, payload_info);
   }
 
